From 2fd12aa6627c48777b56c35825af58c4a793bd8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneup03 <oneup03@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:54:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Create host threads through a HostThread wrapper

Every host thread was a std::thread, which offers no stack size, priority
or core. On the 3DS those matter: libctru threads default to a small
stack, the game threads run recompiled code, and a New 3DS has a second
core for the renderer and the audio microcode. HostThread wraps
std::thread everywhere else and libctru's threadCreate on the 3DS, sized
and placed by a HostThreadSpec per thread kind that a platform layer can
override (set_host_thread_spec_callback). Thread names and runtime
priority changes are no-ops there.
